{"id":"refine_20261108040215554","summary":"No additional edits are needed because the reusable task-6e23da39 rules and exact click sequence were already saved globally.","rationale":"The trajectory shows a completed demonstration, an evidence-backed two-click consolidation rule, and a successful 10-click sequence for the observed layout, all preserved in the newly created global memory as requested.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances can reuse the consolidation strategy and exact coordinates without rediscovering the mechanics or spending extra demonstrations.","appliedEdits":[],"harnessStatePath":"/home/USER/runs/paper/kimi-moonshot-arc3-ha/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1794076728/attempts/0d8c0fd0e444419fb3dd1f61e44b1e19/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20261108062507962","summary":"Update the global task-86c40637 memory with the verified rotation/docking mechanics, demonstration routes, and exact solved layout sequence.","rationale":"The live solve confirmed the general controls and two demonstrated strategies, while failed side-by-side attempts showed that correct object orientation and stacked peg alignment are essential; the existing global memory should therefore be expanded rather than duplicated.","expectedOutcome":"Future task-86c40637 instances can select the appropriate rotation route and directly replay the exact 27-action solution on the recorded layout, avoiding the unsuccessful unrotated side-by-side docking search.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"update","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_86c40637_controls_and_solved_strategy","title":"ARC task-86c40637 rotation/docking mechanics, demo routes, and exact solved layout (general, v2)","content":"Game task-86c40637 is a two-object rotation/docking puzzle. Controls: 1=up, 2=down, 3=left, 4=right; each arrow translates the ACTIVE object by 3 pixels. Action 5 rotates the active object 90 degrees clockwise. Action 6 clicks the OTHER object's orange marker to activate that object and lock the first object cyan/e. Position and rotate both objects so the first object's two orange pegs meet the second object's matching pegs; successful connectors turn green and completion occurs on the final rotation. Demonstration routes: (1) move first object UP x2, RIGHT x4, click the second object's marker, then rotate second x3; (2) move first DOWN x2, LEFT x5, rotate first x3, click second, rotate second x1. Exact solved fresh layout: first black body x2-10,y23-37, right pegs x11-13 at y26-28 and y32-34; second e body x47-55,y26-45, right pegs x56-58 at y32-34 and y38-40. Solution in 27 actions: UP x4, RIGHT x20, ROTATE(5) x1, click (56,32), ROTATE(5) x3. This creates the required stacked alignment. Important failure: merely docking the unrotated objects side-by-side and then rotating/translating the second does not solve, even when some markers appear close or green; reset and use the stacked route above.","path":"arc/task-86c40637","metadata":{"scope":"global","game_id":"task-86c40637","verified":true,"version":2},"reason":"The exact sequence was verified by a live completion, and the generalized routes plus failed approach are reusable across future layouts of this ARC task.","before":{"id":"arc_task_86c40637_controls_and_solved_strategy","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-86c40637 controls and solved strategy","content":"Game task-86c40637: one irregular colored/black piece and one rectangular tray, each with two gray 8 marker pairs. Arrows move the ACTIVE object by 3 cells. Action 5 rotates the active irregular piece 90 degrees. Click inside the rectangular tray interior to toggle activation; click the irregular piece to activate it. Inactive piece=c, inactive tray=e, active object=0. Correct general sequence: activate/move tray roughly under piece if needed; activate piece; place it just above tray with horizontal alignment; rotate until its gray markers are at bottom (usually 3 rotations from initial); markers turn green (3) and level completes. Exact solved layout: initial piece bounds x26..43,y11..25, tray x35..55,y51..61. After some exploration/reset, piece was at base x38,y32 with bottom gray markers x41..43 and47..49,y47..49 after 3 clockwise rotations; tray remained x35..55,y51..61. A final DOWN action moved piece to base y35, markers y50..52 and completed. Efficient inferred solution from fresh initial: activate piece if needed, DOWN 8 and RIGHT 4, rotate 3, then DOWN 1 (total 16 incl activation; initial fresh piece already active so arrows+rotations+final down =16). Demonstration on another layout moved tray RIGHT 12, clicked piece at (51,15), then action5 three times, completing.","path":"general","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{},"source":"agent","created_at":"2026-11-07T21:47:10.125571+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-07T21:47:10.125598+00:00","version":1},"after":{"id":"arc_task_86c40637_controls_and_solved_strategy","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-86c40637 rotation/docking mechanics, demo routes, and exact solved layout (general, v2)","content":"Game task-86c40637 is a two-object rotation/docking puzzle. Controls: 1=up, 2=down, 3=left, 4=right; each arrow translates the ACTIVE object by 3 pixels. Action 5 rotates the active object 90 degrees clockwise. Action 6 clicks the OTHER object's orange marker to activate that object and lock the first object cyan/e. Position and rotate both objects so the first object's two orange pegs meet the second object's matching pegs; successful connectors turn green and completion occurs on the final rotation. Demonstration routes: (1) move first object UP x2, RIGHT x4, click the second object's marker, then rotate second x3; (2) move first DOWN x2, LEFT x5, rotate first x3, click second, rotate second x1. Exact solved fresh layout: first black body x2-10,y23-37, right pegs x11-13 at y26-28 and y32-34; second e body x47-55,y26-45, right pegs x56-58 at y32-34 and y38-40. Solution in 27 actions: UP x4, RIGHT x20, ROTATE(5) x1, click (56,32), ROTATE(5) x3. This creates the required stacked alignment. Important failure: merely docking the unrotated objects side-by-side and then rotating/translating the second does not solve, even when some markers appear close or green; reset and use the stacked route above.","path":"arc/task-86c40637","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","game_id":"task-86c40637","verified":true,"version":2},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-11-07T21:47:10.125571+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-08T06:25:36.014Z","version":2},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/USER/runs/paper/kimi-moonshot-arc3-ha/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1794076728/attempts/0d8c0fd0e444419fb3dd1f61e44b1e19/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
{"id":"refine_20261108093822393","summary":"Persist the newly solved task-86c40637 layout, its concise 16-action route, and the connector-tip interpretation in a separate global memory without overwriting prior routes.","rationale":"The trajectory verified the route through level completion and clarified why earlier apparent overlaps failed; a separate layout entry preserves the existing mechanics, demonstrations, and exact 27-action route.","expectedOutcome":"Future instances of this layout can replay the concise solution directly, while other layouts benefit from tracking only the bright 3x3 connector tips and checking body orientation.","appliedEdits":[{"action":"create","kind":"memory","id":"arc_task_86c40637_solved_fourth_layout_connector_tips","title":"ARC task-86c40637 fourth solved layout: exact 16-action route and connector-tip rule (general, v1)","content":"Game task-86c40637 newly SOLVED layout. Fresh board: active black UP body x5-17,y49-57 with bright orange UP connector region x8-10/x14-16,y40-46; inactive cyan/e body x32-40,y29-47 with bright orange RIGHT connector tips x39-41,y34-36/y40-42. Exact concise successful route from fresh: RIGHT (action 4) 11 times; UP (action 1) twice; click second marker (40,35) with action 6; ROTATE (action 5) once; RIGHT once; UP once. The final UP completes the level (16 actions total). Earlier exploratory four-rotation cycles, net down/up movement, and active-object switches were redundant. Critical interpretation: only the bright orange/cyan 3x3 TIPS are connector targets, not the black/e lower portions of the pegs. After RIGHT x11, UP x2, click (40,35), and one rotation, the second object's orange tips were x38-40/x44-46,y38-40 and the first object's cyan tips were x41-43/x47-49,y38-40. RIGHT aligns x; the extra UP moves the second tips to y35-37, overlapping the actual first tips and completing. Adjacent tips and overlaps involving only non-tip peg/body portions do not count. Green overlap alone is insufficient when body orientations are wrong. Existing memory arc_task_86c40637_controls_and_solved_strategy retains the general controls, demonstrations, and earlier solved routes.","path":"arc/task-86c40637","metadata":{"scope":"global","game":"task-86c40637","status":"solved","route_length":16},"reason":"Stores the independently verified completion route and reusable visual rule without replacing previously saved mechanics and routes.","after":{"id":"arc_task_86c40637_solved_fourth_layout_connector_tips","kind":"memory","title":"ARC task-86c40637 fourth solved layout: exact 16-action route and connector-tip rule (general, v1)","content":"Game task-86c40637 newly SOLVED layout. Fresh board: active black UP body x5-17,y49-57 with bright orange UP connector region x8-10/x14-16,y40-46; inactive cyan/e body x32-40,y29-47 with bright orange RIGHT connector tips x39-41,y34-36/y40-42. Exact concise successful route from fresh: RIGHT (action 4) 11 times; UP (action 1) twice; click second marker (40,35) with action 6; ROTATE (action 5) once; RIGHT once; UP once. The final UP completes the level (16 actions total). Earlier exploratory four-rotation cycles, net down/up movement, and active-object switches were redundant. Critical interpretation: only the bright orange/cyan 3x3 TIPS are connector targets, not the black/e lower portions of the pegs. After RIGHT x11, UP x2, click (40,35), and one rotation, the second object's orange tips were x38-40/x44-46,y38-40 and the first object's cyan tips were x41-43/x47-49,y38-40. RIGHT aligns x; the extra UP moves the second tips to y35-37, overlapping the actual first tips and completing. Adjacent tips and overlaps involving only non-tip peg/body portions do not count. Green overlap alone is insufficient when body orientations are wrong. Existing memory arc_task_86c40637_controls_and_solved_strategy retains the general controls, demonstrations, and earlier solved routes.","path":"arc/task-86c40637","scope":"global","reference":{},"arguments":{},"metadata":{"scope":"global","game":"task-86c40637","status":"solved","route_length":16},"source":"refine","created_at":"2026-11-08T09:38:56.852Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T09:38:56.852Z","version":1},"applied":true}],"harnessStatePath":"/home/USER/runs/paper/kimi-moonshot-arc3-ha/.workbench/runs/adhoc-primeagentlearner-1794076728/attempts/0d8c0fd0e444419fb3dd1f61e44b1e19/system/state/agent/harness/harness_state.json","scope":"global"}
